@startuml settlement-domain-relations
title settlement.domain — model relations

' Names and relations only. Column-level properties are a later task.
' A solid arrow that leaves this context is an id. Contexts do not share tables.
' A dashed arrow is a ledger posting this context depends on.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
hide empty members

package settlement {
  package domain {
    class ClearingItem
    class Settlement
  }
}

package card <<external>> {
  package domain {
    class Purchase
    class AuthorizationHold
  }
}

package ledger <<external>> {
  package domain {
    class JournalEntry
  }
}

Purchase "1" <-- "0..1" ClearingItem : purchase
AuthorizationHold "1" <-- "0..1" ClearingItem : hold
Purchase "1" <-- "0..1" Settlement : purchase
Settlement ..> JournalEntry : merchant settlement\n2300 debit, 2200 and 4100 credit

note bottom of ClearingItem
  The merchant's confirmation of the authorized amount.
  Links the hold to the purchase.
  Present once the purchase is CLEARED.
  Inserting it does not write the journal.
end note

note bottom of Settlement
  The movement from Settlement Suspense (2300)
  to the merchant deposit (2200) and Interchange Income (4100).
  Present once the purchase is POSTED.
  The balanced lines belong to one JournalEntry in ledger.
  Merchant owns 2200; this model does not own that account.
end note

@enduml
